Subject: [PATCH] spi: k1x-qspi: balance the probe runtime PM reference

Probe initializes the hardware and then drops a runtime PM reference it
never acquired, producing "Runtime PM usage count underflow!" immediately
after the NOR device is registered. It also calls pm_runtime_set_active()
after enabling runtime PM, when that helper returns -EAGAIN.

Set the active state before enabling runtime PM and hold a probe reference
while registering the controller and sysfs attributes. Release it on the
successful path after marking the device busy; the existing error path
balances it with pm_runtime_put_noidle().

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-k1x-qspi.c
@@ -1568,8 +1568,10 @@
 	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(&pdev->dev, QSPI_AUTOSUSPEND_TIMEOUT);
 	pm_suspend_ignore_children(&pdev->dev, 1);
-	pm_runtime_enable(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_active(&pdev->dev);
+	/* Keep the initialized controller active until probe has finished. */
+	pm_runtime_get_noresume(&pdev->dev);
+	pm_runtime_enable(&pdev->dev);
 
 	ctlr->dev.of_node = np;
 	ctlr->dev.parent = &pdev->dev;
@@ -1579,8 +1581,6 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_destroy_mutex;
 
-	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
-
 #ifdef CONFIG_SYSFS
 	ret = sysfs_create_group(&(pdev->dev.kobj),
 			(const struct attribute_group *)(&qspi_dev_group));
@@ -1591,6 +1591,8 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
+	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(&pdev->dev);
+	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 	return 0;
 
 err_destroy_mutex:
